{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-284",
  "title": "Podcast Interview Notes",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Podcast Interview Notes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Based on the interview, the main topics discussed are:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**1. The Passion for Whole Grains:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Nan Kohler's mission is to change the public's perception of whole grain flour, highlighting its diverse flavors, aromas, and textures."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "She advocates for treating flour as a primary flavor ingredient, much like wine grapes or coffee beans, rather than just a structural component in baking."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**2. The State of Modern Flour and the Local Grain Movement:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Discussion on how industrialization led to the dominance of bland, refined white flour for mass-produced goods like sandwich bread."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The rise of a regional grain movement, involving farmers, millers, and bakers, aimed at reintroducing heirloom grains and more flavorful, nutritious flours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The challenges of this movement, including misleading labeling terms like \"whole grain\" and \"whole wheat,\" and the need for greater transparency."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**3. Building a Niche Business (Grist & Toll):**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The journey of starting a unique business, specifically an urban flour mill, which involves sourcing specialized equipment, navigating city regulations, and establishing a supply chain with local farmers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The challenges of being a small business owner, from managing daily operations and finances to dealing with unexpected problems."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**4. Baking with Whole Grain Flour:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-18",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Practical advice on how to adapt recipes for whole grain flours, which are \"thirstier\" and behave differently than refined all-purpose flour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The importance of experimentation and education for both home bakers and professionals looking to incorporate these flours."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**5. Personal and Professional Philosophy:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-22",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The importance of taking a leap of faith, being courageous, and staying curious."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-23",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How to stay motivated through challenges by focusing on the purpose and meaning behind the work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-24",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Success is defined not just by the final outcome but by the process of trying, learning, and contributing to a larger change."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Based on the interview, Nan Kohler's biggest pain points stem from the fact that her business is not just about selling a product, but about pioneering a fundamental change in the food system. Her challenges can be grouped into a few key areas:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. The Educational and Perceptual Hurdle"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is a constant and foundational challenge."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-30",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Changing Perceptions:** Her primary mission is \"changing everyone's perceptions of whole grain\" and re-educating a public that has been \"trained not to think about flour\" as a flavorful, key ingredient."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-31",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Misleading Terminology:** She is frustrated by the dilution and misuse of terms like \"whole grain,\" \"whole wheat,\" and \"artisan.\" She notes that an Instagram photo of \"spelt bread\" might only contain 10% spelt, which creates false expectations and makes it harder to explain the value of her 100% whole grain products."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-32",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Overcoming History:** She is fighting against \"200 to 300 years of the world's worst, unappealing whole-grain flour,\" trying to get consumers to forget their past negative experiences and fall in love with what real whole grain can be."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Systemic and Industry-Wide Challenges"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is what she calls her \"biggest professional challenge\" because it's \"so much bigger than me.\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-36",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Lack of Shared Risk:** She points out a \"tremendous disconnect\" where small farmers are expected to bear all the financial risk of growing diverse, organic, and heirloom grains. The burden of investing in land, seeds, and equipment falls on them, while bakers and consumers are not yet structured to share that cost upfront."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-37",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Immature Infrastructure:** The ecosystem for local grain is still developing. This means sourcing equipment is difficult (it has to be imported), finding collaborators is slow, and there isn't a streamlined system for everything from seed cleaning to high-volume production."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-38",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**The Need for More Collaborators:** Nan feels the movement can't succeed with just a few pioneers. She needs more farmers, more urban millers, and more bakers to \"jump\" in and commit to the change to create a sustainable marketplace."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Logistical and Personal Toll of a Pioneer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "These are the day-to-day realities of running a unique, demanding business."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-42",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Inability to Meet Potential:** One of her biggest frustrations is being \"tied to the mill every single day\" just to keep up with production. This limits her ability to develop educational content (videos, blogs, recipes) that she knows there is a huge demand for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-43",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Constant Problem-Solving:** As a sole entrepreneur, she can't just be a miller. She has to be a mechanic, a sourcing expert, a logistics coordinator, and a marketer. The challenges are relentless and constantly shifting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-44",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Burnout and Isolation:** She admits that the work is intense, she hasn't had a vacation in five years, and on some days, she feels defeated. The burden of being at the forefront of a movement is immense."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "#"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}